{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Don't [F]let your sweet love die like flowers in the [Bb]fall
Don't [C]take away the smiles and leave a [F]tear
My [F]heart believes in you, please say you love me [Bb]too
Don't [C]leave me now to face the lonely [F]years
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [F]drifted all alone, no one to call my [Bb]own
And [C]then you came like an angel from the [F]sky
You [F]said we'd never part, don't leave and break my [Bb]heart
[C]Don’t say goodbye, don't let your sweet love [F]die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
When flowers fade away they'll bloom again someday
Will you love me when the rose buds open wide
Or is your kiss to be only a memory
I need you so, don't let your sweet love die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Don't let your sweet love die like flowers in the fall
Without you, life would be like death to me
I've grown so used to you, I can't believe we're through
Don’t say goodbye, don't your sweet love die
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Don't let your sweet love die like flowers in the fall
Don't take away the smiles and leave a tear
My heart believes in you, please say you love me too
Don’t say goodbye, don't let your sweet love die
{end_of_verse}
